    <section class="msc-learn-key-terms"><h2>Key Terms</h2><dl><div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Glossary</dt><dd>An index of concise preferred definitions linked to canonical long-form MSC Learn destinations.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Preferred term</dt><dd>The primary reader-facing label for one glossary concept.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Canonical editorial destination</dt><dd>The guide, hub, route, or glossary package that owns the complete explanation.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Planning handle</dt><dd>An internal routing handle that does not prove a public page exists.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Letter anchor</dt><dd>An alphabetical target created only when at least one term uses that letter.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Status-sensitive term</dt><dd>A term whose proposal, implementation, software, provider, legal, market, or maturity state can change.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Protocol status</dt><dd>The documented state of a proposal or specification, kept separate from activation, deployment, and adoption.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Publication-time renewal</dt><dd>Fresh verification of mutable claims immediately before public release.</dd></div></dl></section>
